 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "On a perpendicular coordinate plane, find the two coordinates of the midpoint $C$ of the straight segment $AB$: $A({=x1}, {=y1})$ and $B({=x2}, {=y2})$. Write your answer as $(x, y)$.",
 "solution": [
  "$A({=x1}, {=y1})$ and $B({=x2}, {=y2})$.",
  "$x = \\frac{{=x1} + {=paren(x2)}}{2} = {=mx}$",
  "$y = \\frac{{=y1} + {=paren(y2)}}{2} = {=my}$",
  "The midpoint is $C({=mx}, {=my})$."
 ],
